<title>UK: NYNEX revenue increases 78 pct in year.</title>
<headline>NYNEX revenue increases 78 pct in year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>					 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating cash flow    loss 5.6	     vs loss 46.7</p>
<p>Revenue		    151		    vs 85</p>
<p>Net loss under UK GAAP loss 63.1	    vs loss 72.1</p>
<p>Net loss under US GAAP loss 22.85	   vs loss 439,000</p>
<p>Residential telephony revenue</p>
<p>				70.6		   vs 36.4</p>
<p>Cable television revenue</p>
<p>				62.4		   vs 38.7</p>
<p>Business telephony revenue</p>
<p>				13.1		   vs5.25</p>
<p> Operating costs	  156.8		  vs 131.7</p>
<p>				 (subscribers in thousands)</p>
<p>Residential telephony	   349,260	  vs 232,511</p>
<p>Business telephony		33,287	   vs 14.260</p>
<p> Cable television customers    268,519	  vs 197,004</p>
<p>NOTE - NYNEX CableComms Group Plc, which provides cable telephony and cable television in the UK, is an affiliate of U.S. cable group Nynex Corp.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
